sn55.23:8.4 | S: “Sir, some instigation of a legal proceeding might come up. The Buddha might take one side, and the Saṅgha of monks the other. | T: “There is the case, lord, where a certain Dhamma issue might arise, with the Blessed One on one side and with the Saṅgha of monks on the other side.
sn55.23:8.5 | S: I’d side with the Buddha. | T: Whichever side the Blessed One would be on, that’s the side where I would be.
